      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The Statement requires the length identity for all 0≤r≤q≤L, while step 6.1 proceeds: “Now let r=ρ₀<…<ρ_N=q be a partition of [r,q].” No such strict partition exists when r=q. The singleton-interval convention in the Statement immediately supplies the identity in that case, so this is an omitted endpoint branch.",
