      "evidence": "The induction treats the mixed case only as “x∈ι_e(C_e), y∈Z₁,” while claiming injectivity of z↦d₀(x,z) for every ordered pair. For the opposite ordering, swapping endpoints gives injectivity of distance from y; to obtain the claimed injectivity from x one also needs d₀(x,z)=d₀(x,y)−d₀(y,z) for z∈I(x,y). This follows immediately from the definition of I, so the gap is nonfatal.",
